## Summary

The registration-date business-day logic lives in the OfficeFloor "owner create" function pipeline under `.../rest/function/owner/`. The core adjuster is `BusinessDays.rollForward(...)`, applied by `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate`.

### 1. The class/method that adjusts a registration date to a business day

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDays.java` — package-private helper. `rollForward` loops while the date is SATURDAY/SUNDAY, adding a day (so weekends roll forward to Monday). Note: it handles **weekends only, not holidays** (see the mismatch note below).

```java
final class BusinessDays {
    private BusinessDays() {}

    /** The given date if it is a weekday, otherwise the next Monday. */
    static LocalDate rollForward(LocalDate date) {
        while (date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SATURDAY || date.getDayOfWeek() == DayOfWeek.SUNDAY) {
            date = date.plusDays(1);
        }
        return date;
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate.java` — the OfficeFloor function that calls it. Defaults a missing date to `LocalDate.now()`, then rolls forward and stores the adjusted value back on the `Owner`:

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    LocalDate effective = owner.getRegistrationDate() != null ? owner.getRegistrationDate() : LocalDate.now();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDays.rollForward(effective));
}
```

### 2. Tests for that logic

There is **no dedicated unit test** for `BusinessDays` or `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate` (grep of `src/test` for those class names returned nothing). The only coverage is black-box acceptance testing:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — asserts the invariant that a default `registrationDate` is never Saturday/Sunday:

